# A whole SQL query: one DS0105 with the equivalent pipeline (not machine-applicable: worth a look).
mode: syntax
---- query
SELECT customerId, amount FROM orders WHERE amount > 10
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..56
  PIPELINE@0..55
    ERROR@0..55
      IDENT@0..6 "SELECT"
      WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
      IDENT@7..17 "customerId"
      COMMA@17..18 ","
      WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
      IDENT@19..25 "amount"
      WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
      IDENT@26..30 "FROM"
      WHITESPACE@30..31 " "
      IDENT@31..37 "orders"
      WHITESPACE@37..38 " "
      IDENT@38..43 "WHERE"
      WHITESPACE@43..44 " "
      IDENT@44..50 "amount"
      WHITESPACE@50..51 " "
      GT@51..52 ">"
      WHITESPACE@52..53 " "
      LONG@53..55 "10"
  WHITESPACE@55..56 "\n"

error[DS0105]: `SELECT ... FROM` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> query:1:1
  |
1 | SELECT customerId, amount FROM orders WHERE amount > 10
  | ^^^^^^                    ---- in DataScript the table comes first
  | |
  | this is SQL
  |
  = help: start with the table and pipe it into operators: `orders | where amount > 10 | project customerId, amount`
